# CoT (Cursor on Target) event XML. Public.
# `version` is a constant of the schema. `start` is written from the report
# time, as `time` is. `stale` has no value the pack can state: how long a report
# stays valid is the sender's policy, so the caller supplies `stale_ms`
# (`convert` context, CLI `--set stale_ms=<epoch ms>`).
# The schema requires `type` and the point's `hae`, `ce` and `le`; the `default`
# lines give the values that say "not known": 9999999 for the three numbers and
# a-u-X (atom, unknown affiliation, other) for the type. `how` is required too,
# but the schema names no value for "not known", so it has no default.
format  cot-xml
version 0.5.0
distribution public
source  "Cursor on Target event schema (MITRE, public release); field use cross-checked against pytak"
uses    track
wire    xml
root    event
const   @version  2.0
field   track.scoped_id  @uid                 string
field   uid       @uid                        string
field   type      @type                       string
field   time_ms   @time                       iso8601_ms
field   time_ms   @start                      iso8601_ms
field   stale_ms  @stale                      iso8601_ms
field   how       @how                        string
field   access    @access                     string
field   lat       point/@lat                  float
field   lon       point/@lon                  float
field   hae       point/@hae                  float  absent 9999999,9999999.0
field   ce        point/@ce                   float  absent 9999999,9999999.0
field   le        point/@le                   float  absent 9999999,9999999.0
field   callsign  detail/contact/@callsign    string
field   course    detail/track/@course        float
field   speed_ms  detail/track/@speed         float
# The sender's text of the two instants, after the lines that parse them, so
# a changed time_ms or stale_ms is what encode writes (ruling 16 of 0.5).
field   time_text     @time              string
field   stale_text    @stale             string
field   display_name  detail/uid/@Droid  string
default type      a-u-X
default hae       9999999
default ce        9999999
default le        9999999
